1
00:00:01,627 --> 00:00:02,962
ALL RIGHT, HERE WE GO.

2
00:00:03,002 --> 00:00:05,297
1999. THE
YEAR OF JOEY.

3
00:00:05,339 --> 00:00:06,841
YEAH.

4
00:00:06,882 --> 00:00:08,550
WE'RE VERY HAPPY FOR YOU.

5
00:00:08,592 --> 00:00:10,218
WHAT'S THE
MATTER?

6
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:12,805
WE WANTED TO KISS AT
MIDNIGHT, BUT NOBODY
ELSE IS GOING TO

7
00:00:12,847 --> 00:00:13,889
SO, YOU KNOW...

8
00:00:13,931 --> 00:00:16,350
ALL RIGHT. I'LL
TAKE CARE OF IT.

9
00:00:16,391 --> 00:00:17,351
JOEY...

10
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:20,145
33... 32... 31...

11
00:00:20,187 --> 00:00:21,689
ROSS! ROSS!
ROSS, LISTEN.

12
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:23,816
WHO ARE YOU KISSING AT MIDNIGHT?
RACHEL OR PHOEBE?

13
00:00:23,858 --> 00:00:26,360
WHAT?
YOU GOT TO KISS
SOMEONE. CAN'T
KISS YOUR SISTER.

14
00:00:26,401 --> 00:00:27,987
WELL, WHO'S GOING
TO KISS MY SISTER?

15
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:29,989
CHANDLER.
OH, MAN. REALLY?

16
00:00:30,029 --> 00:00:32,157
WHO WOULD YOU
RATHER HAVE KISS
HER? ME OR CHANDLER?

17
00:00:32,199 --> 00:00:33,534
THAT'S A GOOD POINT.
YEAH.

18
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:35,786
UH, WELL SINCE I HAVE
THAT WHOLE HISTORY

19
00:00:35,828 --> 00:00:37,329
WITH RACHEL,
I GUESS PHOEBE.

20
00:00:37,371 --> 00:00:38,539
OKAY. GREAT.

21
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,207
PHEEBS! PHEEBS!
LISTEN--

22
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:42,501
ROSS WANTS TO KISS YOU
AT MIDNIGHT.

23
00:00:42,543 --> 00:00:43,585
IT'S SO OBVIOUS.

24
00:00:43,627 --> 00:00:45,253
WHY DOESN'T HE JUST ASK?

25
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:46,922
RACHE... RACHE, LISTEN.

26
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:48,423
I'M GOING TO KISS
YOU AT MIDNIGHT.

27
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:49,508
WHAT?
EVERYONE'S GOT TO.

28
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:50,885
CAN'T KISS ROSS.
YOU GOT HISTORY.

29
00:00:50,926 --> 00:00:52,219
SO?
SO, WHO WOULD
YOU RATHER

30
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:53,804
HAVE KISS YOU,
ME OR CHANDLER?

31
00:00:53,846 --> 00:00:54,805
OH, GOOD POINT.

32
00:00:54,847 --> 00:00:56,056
YEAH.

33
00:00:56,097 --> 00:00:58,767
All:
THREE... TWO... ONE...

34
00:00:58,809 --> 00:01:00,352
HAPPY NEW YEAR!

35
00:01:00,394 --> 00:01:02,980
( blowing party horns )

36
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,735
HAPPY NEW YEAR.

37
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:08,944
HAPPY NEW YEAR.

38
00:01:08,986 --> 00:01:10,696
HAPPY NEW YEAR,
PHEEBS.
YOU, TOO.

39
00:01:10,738 --> 00:01:12,113
HAPPY NEW YEAR, JOEY.

40
00:01:12,155 --> 00:01:14,449
SO, THAT DO
ANYTHING FOR YOU?

41
00:01:21,832 --> 00:01:26,879
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

42
00:01:26,921 --> 00:01:29,256
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

43
00:01:29,297 --> 00:01:32,175
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

44
00:01:32,217 --> 00:01:36,597
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

45
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:39,558
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

46
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,602
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

47
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:45,230
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

48
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:47,315
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

49
00:01:47,357 --> 00:01:49,944
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

50
00:01:49,985 --> 00:01:52,153
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

51
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:55,365
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

52
00:01:55,407 --> 00:01:58,869
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

53
00:02:03,415 --> 00:02:04,374
YOU KNOW WHAT?

54
00:02:04,416 --> 00:02:05,459
I'M GOING TO GO

55
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,877
OUT ON A LIMB AND SAY

56
00:02:06,919 --> 00:02:08,378
NO DIVORCES IN '99!

57
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:09,463
YEAH, BABY!

58
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:11,339
( blowing horns )

59
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:13,508
BUT YOU'RE DIVORCE
ISN'T EVEN FINAL YET.

60
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,260
JUST THE ONE DIVORCE IN '99!

61
00:02:15,302 --> 00:02:16,261
YEAH, BABY!

62
00:02:16,303 --> 00:02:17,345
( blowing horns )

63
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:18,513
YOU KNOW WHAT?

64
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:20,348
I AM GOING TO BE HAPPY
THIS YEAR.

65
00:02:20,390 --> 00:02:22,684
I AM GOING TO MAKE MYSELF HAPPY.

66
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:25,353
DO YOU WANT US TO
LEAVE THE ROOM OR...?

67
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:27,689
EVERY DAY, I AM GOING
TO DO ONE THING

68
00:02:27,731 --> 00:02:29,524
I HAVE NEVER DONE BEFORE.

69
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:32,527
THAT, MY FRIENDS,
IS MY NEW YEAR'S RESOLUTION.

70
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:34,195
OOH! THAT'S A GOOD ONE.

71
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:35,489
YEAH.

72
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:37,407
MINE IS TO PILOT
A COMMERCIAL JET.

73
00:02:37,449 --> 00:02:38,617
OH...

74
00:02:38,659 --> 00:02:40,201
THAT'S A GOOD ONE, TOO, PHEEBS.

75
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:42,830
NOW ALL YOU HAVE TO DO
IS FIND A PLANELOAD OF PEOPLE

76
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:45,248
WHOSE RESOLUTION
IS TO PLUMMET TO THEIR DEATHS.

77
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:48,752
MAYBE YOUR RESOLUTION
SHOULD BE NOT TO MAKE
FUN OF YOUR FRIENDS

78
00:02:48,794 --> 00:02:50,587
ESPECIALLY THE ONES
WHO MAY SOON

79
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:53,548
BE FLYING YOU
TO EUROPE FOR FREE
ON THEIR OWN PLANE.

80
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:56,010
SHE HAS A BETTER CHANCE
OF SPROUTING WINGS

81
00:02:56,051 --> 00:02:57,385
AND FLYING UP YOUR NOSE

82
00:02:57,427 --> 00:02:59,930
THAN YOU DO
OF NOT MAKING FUN OF US.

83
00:02:59,972 --> 00:03:02,766
IN FACT, I'LL BET YOU 50 BUCKS
YOU CAN'T GO THE WHOLE YEAR

84
00:03:02,808 --> 00:03:04,059
WITHOUT MAKING FUN OF US.

85
00:03:04,101 --> 00:03:05,769
YOU KNOW WHAT?
BETTER YET-- A WEEK.

86
00:03:05,811 --> 00:03:07,521
I'LL TAKE THAT BET, MY FRIEND.

87
00:03:07,562 --> 00:03:09,314
AND YOU KNOW WHAT?

88
00:03:09,356 --> 00:03:12,651
PAYING ME THE 50 BUCKS CAN BE
THE "NEW THING" YOU DO THAT DAY.

89
00:03:14,653 --> 00:03:16,655
AND IT STARTS RIGHT NOW.

90
00:03:17,948 --> 00:03:19,950
ALL RIGHT,
MY NEW YEAR'S RESOLUTION

91
00:03:19,992 --> 00:03:21,785
IS TO LEARN HOW
TO PLAY GUITAR.

92
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:23,453
REALLY? HOW COME?

93
00:03:23,495 --> 00:03:25,789
WELL, YOU KNOW THOSE,
UH, SPECIAL SKILLS

94
00:03:25,831 --> 00:03:27,374
I HAVE LISTED
ON MY RESUME?

95
00:03:27,415 --> 00:03:30,961
WELL, I WOULD LOVE IT
IF ONE OF THOSE WAS TRUE.

96
00:03:31,003 --> 00:03:33,212
DO YOU WANT ME TO TEACH YOU?
I'M A GREAT TEACHER.

97
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:35,132
OH, REALLY? WHO HAVE YOU TAUGHT?

98
00:03:35,174 --> 00:03:37,425
WELL, I TAUGHT ME
AND I LOVED ME.

99
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:39,636
OH, THAT'D BE GREAT.

100
00:03:39,678 --> 00:03:41,055
YEAH. THANKS, PHEEBS.

101
00:03:41,096 --> 00:03:43,348
OH, LOOK--
BLAIR FORGOT HER GLASSES

102
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:45,392
AND SHE'S GOING
TO REALLY BE
NEEDING THESE

103
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:47,394
TO KEEP AN
EYE ON THAT
BOYFRIEND

104
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:48,896
WHO, FROM WHAT I HEAR

105
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:51,231
NEEDS TO KEEP HIS STAPLER
IN HIS DESK DRAWER

106
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:53,734
IF YOU KNOW WHAT I'M
TALKING ABOUT.

107
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:56,028
HEY, RACHE, MAYBE YOUR
RESOLUTION SHOULD BE

108
00:03:56,070 --> 00:03:57,445
TO, UM... GOSSIP LESS.

109
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:59,531
I DON'T GOSSIP.

110
00:03:59,573 --> 00:04:01,116
( sarcastic chuckles )

111
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:04,203
MAYBE SOMETIMES
I FIND OUT THINGS

112
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:07,664
OR I HEAR SOMETHING AND I
PASS THAT INFORMATION ON.

113
00:04:07,706 --> 00:04:10,375
YOU KNOW, KIND OF LIKE
A PUBLIC SERVICE.

114
00:04:10,417 --> 00:04:12,127
DOESN'T MEAN
I'M A GOSSIP.

115
00:04:12,169 --> 00:04:14,838
I MEAN, WOULD YOU
CALL TED KOPPEL A GOSSIP?

116
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,590
WELL, IF TED KOPPEL TALKED ABOUT

117
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:19,342
HIS CO-WORKER'S BOTCHED
BOOB JOBS, YEAH, I WOULD.

118
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:21,428
THEY WERE LIKE THIS!

119
00:04:27,059 --> 00:04:28,393
I'LL SEE YOU
TOMORROW.

120
00:04:28,435 --> 00:04:29,686
OKAY.

121
00:04:30,896 --> 00:04:31,897
HEY.

122
00:04:31,939 --> 00:04:33,023
HEY
HEY.

123
00:04:33,065 --> 00:04:34,733
I JUST ASKED THAT GIRL OUT.

124
00:04:34,775 --> 00:04:35,734
NICE.

125
00:04:35,776 --> 00:04:36,818
NICE... YEAH.

126
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:38,195
IS THAT PART
OF YOUR RESOLUTION?

127
00:04:38,237 --> 00:04:39,487
YOUR "NEW THING"
FOR TODAY?

128
00:04:39,529 --> 00:04:40,655
YES, IT IS.

129
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:41,740
SEE?

130
00:04:41,782 --> 00:04:43,200
"ELIZABETH...

131
00:04:43,242 --> 00:04:45,202
...HORNSWOGGLE"?

132
00:04:47,079 --> 00:04:48,329
THAT'S RIGHT.

133
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:52,167
ELIZABETH... HORNSWOGGLE.

134
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:55,921
HORN... SWOGGLE?

135
00:04:56,964 --> 00:04:58,298
YOU OKAY, CHANDLER?

136
00:04:58,339 --> 00:04:59,591
IS THERE SOMETHING...?

137
00:04:59,633 --> 00:05:02,136
SOMETHING FUNNY
ABOUT THAT NAME?

138
00:05:02,177 --> 00:05:04,179
NO. NO. I JUST THINK
THAT MAYBE I'VE...

139
00:05:04,221 --> 00:05:05,931
I'VE HEARD IT SOMEWHERE BEFORE.

140
00:05:08,349 --> 00:05:11,186
OH, REALLY?
WHERE?

141
00:05:12,229 --> 00:05:14,148
SOMEWHERE FUNNY, I'LL BET.

142
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:16,733
HEY...

143
00:05:16,775 --> 00:05:17,734
GUESS WHAT?

144
00:05:17,776 --> 00:05:19,194
I HAVE A DATE
WITH, UH...

145
00:05:19,236 --> 00:05:21,613
ELIZABETH
HORNSWOGGLE.

146
00:05:23,282 --> 00:05:24,407
HORNSWOGGLE?

147
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:27,244
OH, THIS MUST BE KILLING YOU.

148
00:05:27,286 --> 00:05:28,578
SEE YOU LATER.

149
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,038
SEE YOU.

150
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:32,582
ALL RIGHT, PHEEBS, I AM READY
FOR MY FIRST LESSON.

151
00:05:32,624 --> 00:05:33,583
OKAY.

152
00:05:33,625 --> 00:05:34,584
OH, NO, NO.

153
00:05:34,626 --> 00:05:36,170
YOU DON'T TOUCH
THE GUITAR.

154
00:05:36,211 --> 00:05:37,921
NO. NO. FIRST,
YOU LEARN HERE.

155
00:05:37,963 --> 00:05:39,214
THEN YOU LEARN HERE.

156
00:05:39,256 --> 00:05:41,258
OH... OKAY.

157
00:05:42,383 --> 00:05:43,342
OKAY--

158
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:44,427
LESSON ONE.

159
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:46,013
CHORDS.

160
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:49,975
NOW, UM, I DON'T KNOW
THE ACTUAL NAMES OF THE CHORDS

161
00:05:50,017 --> 00:05:52,102
UM, BUT I-I-I

162
00:05:52,144 --> 00:05:54,229
MADE UP NAMES
FOR THE WAY MY HAND LOOKS

163
00:05:54,271 --> 00:05:55,438
WHILE I'M DOING THEM.

164
00:05:56,815 --> 00:05:57,816
SO, THEN

165
00:05:57,858 --> 00:05:59,901
THIS IS "BEAR CLAW."

166
00:06:00,944 --> 00:06:03,155
OKAY. UM,
"TURKEY LEG..."

167
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:06,449
AND "OLD LADY."

168
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:12,247
WHAT AN INTERESTING APPROACH
TO GUITAR INSTRUCTION.

169
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:15,917
YOU KNOW, SOME MIGHT
FIND IT AMUSING.

170
00:06:15,959 --> 00:06:17,669
I, MYSELF, FIND IT REGULAR.

171
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:23,967
HEY, EVERYBODY.
RACHEL WAS SO
GOOD TODAY.

172
00:06:24,009 --> 00:06:25,384
SHE DIDN'T GOSSIP AT ALL.

173
00:06:25,426 --> 00:06:27,179
I DIDN'T.
EVEN WHEN I FOUND OUT...

174
00:06:27,221 --> 00:06:28,889
UM... ALL RIGHT...

175
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,224
WELL, LET'S JUST SAY

176
00:06:30,265 --> 00:06:32,184
I FOUND OUT SOMETHING
ABOUT SOMEONE

177
00:06:32,226 --> 00:06:34,895
AND LET'S JUST SAY...
SHE'S GOING TO KEEP IT.

178
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:37,898
HEY, PHEEBS.

179
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:39,191
CHECK THIS OUT.

180
00:06:43,278 --> 00:06:45,864
OOH! YOU-YOU NAILED
THE "OLD LADY."

181
00:06:45,906 --> 00:06:47,241
OH!

182
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:51,786
YEAH...

183
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:53,038
YEAH. LISTEN, SO--

184
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,455
I THOUGHT I WAS
GETTING BETTER

185
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:55,665
SO, ON MY WAY HOME TODAY

186
00:06:55,707 --> 00:06:57,376
I STOPPED BY THIS
GUITAR STORE AND...

187
00:06:57,416 --> 00:06:59,502
DID YOU-DID YOU TOUCH
ANY OF THE GUITARS

188
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:00,628
WHILE YOU WERE THERE?

189
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,339
DID YOU?

190
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:06,093
NO.

191
00:07:07,177 --> 00:07:09,012
GIVE ME YOUR HANDS.

192
00:07:10,347 --> 00:07:11,765
STRINGS.

193
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:13,183
GIVE IT.

194
00:07:13,225 --> 00:07:14,393
PICK.

195
00:07:14,433 --> 00:07:15,476
OH!

196
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:19,606
DO YOU WANT TO LEARN
TO PLAY GUITAR?

197
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:20,607
YES.

198
00:07:20,648 --> 00:07:22,109
THEN DON'T TOUCH ONE!

199
00:07:24,111 --> 00:07:25,195
HI.

200
00:07:25,237 --> 00:07:26,363
HI!

201
00:07:26,405 --> 00:07:27,906
HI, BEN!

202
00:07:27,948 --> 00:07:30,242
AUNTIE MONICA!

203
00:07:30,284 --> 00:07:32,411
ROSS IS WEARING LEATHER PANTS!

204
00:07:36,748 --> 00:07:40,668
DOES NOBODY ELSE SEE
THAT ROSS IS WEARING
LEATHER PANTS?

205
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:43,546
SOMEONE! COMMENT
ON THE PANTS!

206
00:07:44,965 --> 00:07:45,966
THEY'RE
VERY NICE.

207
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:47,050
I REALLY
LIKE THEM.

208
00:07:47,092 --> 00:07:48,551
YEAH.
NICE STUFF.

209
00:07:50,011 --> 00:07:52,097
NOT WHAT I
HAD IN MIND.

210
00:07:52,139 --> 00:07:53,807
SEE, PEOPLE LIKE ROSS

211
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:56,268
DON'T GENERALLY WEAR
THESE TYPES OF PANTS.

212
00:07:56,310 --> 00:07:58,686
YOU SEE, THEY'RE
VERY TIGHT.

213
00:07:58,728 --> 00:08:01,940
MAYBE THERE'S
SOMETHING IN
THAT AREA.

214
00:08:01,982 --> 00:08:03,442
THEY LOOK GOOD.
I LIKE THEM.

215
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,443
WAY TO GO.

216
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:05,860
THEY LOOK
GREAT.

217
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:07,695
WHERE DID YOU
GET THEM?

218
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:10,073
SEE, I... I NEEDED
A NEW THING FOR TODAY

219
00:08:10,115 --> 00:08:12,326
AND THERE'S THIS
LEATHER STORE I GO BY

220
00:08:12,367 --> 00:08:13,910
THAT ALWAYS
SMELLS SO GOOD.

221
00:08:13,952 --> 00:08:15,578
AND I THOUGHT
TO MYSELF, WOW.

222
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,122
YOU KNOW,
I'VE NEVER OWNED

223
00:08:17,164 --> 00:08:21,709
A REALLY GOOD-SMELLING
PAIR OF PANTS BEFORE.

224
00:08:24,296 --> 00:08:25,797
OH, COME ON!

225
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:32,053
OKAY, SERIOUSLY,
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

226
00:08:32,095 --> 00:08:33,430
AWFUL.
ABSOLUTELY AWFUL.

227
00:08:33,472 --> 00:08:34,555
YEAH. AWFUL.

228
00:08:37,809 --> 00:08:38,935
HEY, WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

229
00:08:38,977 --> 00:08:39,978
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

230
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,229
IT'S MY NEW YEAR'S
RESOLUTION.

231
00:08:41,271 --> 00:08:42,730
TO BLIND MY CHILD?

232
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:45,066
NO. TO TAKE MORE
PICTURES OF ALL
OF US TOGETHER.

233
00:08:45,108 --> 00:08:47,361
I MEAN, I REALLY
THINK IT'S THE
BEST RESOLUTION

234
00:08:47,402 --> 00:08:49,279
BECAUSE EVERYONE
CAN ENJOY THE
PICTURES.

235
00:08:49,321 --> 00:08:52,157
WELL, EVERYONE WILL
ENJOY MY MUSIC AS WELL.

236
00:09:03,168 --> 00:09:04,544
Ross:
OH, MY GOD.

237
00:09:04,585 --> 00:09:07,714
THESE PANTS-- I'M BURNING UP.

238
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:11,759
SHE WANTS TO SNUGGLE NOW?

239
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:13,845
WHAT? IS SHE TRYING TO KILL ME?

240
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:16,515
IT'S LIKE A VOLCANO IN HERE.

241
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:19,142
ARE YOU HOT?

242
00:09:19,184 --> 00:09:20,810
NO.

243
00:09:20,852 --> 00:09:23,646
OKAY. MUST JUST
BE ME, THEN.

244
00:09:28,735 --> 00:09:30,320
( pants squeaking )

245
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:39,704
THAT WAS JUST THE PANTS
ON THE COUCH.

246
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:45,085
UM, HEY, DO YOU-DO YOU MIND
IF I USE YOUR BATHROOM?

247
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:46,211
OH, GO AHEAD.

248
00:09:46,253 --> 00:09:47,295
THANKS.

249
00:09:47,337 --> 00:09:48,838
( pants squeaking )

250
00:10:03,353 --> 00:10:05,272
( sighs )

251
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:26,834
( falsetto ):
AH...

252
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:28,169
HEY!

253
00:10:28,211 --> 00:10:29,837
MY FAVORITE
PART'S COMING UP!

254
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:31,131
'KAY.

255
00:10:48,064 --> 00:10:49,649
OH, MY GOD!

256
00:10:53,612 --> 00:10:54,737
"TIGER."

257
00:10:54,779 --> 00:10:56,156
"DRAGON."

258
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:58,074
"ICEBERG."

259
00:10:58,116 --> 00:11:01,202
JOSEPH, DID YOU EVEN
STUDY AT ALL LAST NIGHT?

260
00:11:01,244 --> 00:11:03,079
YES. YES, I DID.

261
00:11:03,121 --> 00:11:04,539
THEN DO "ICEBERG."

262
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:06,916
"G" SHARP.

263
00:11:06,958 --> 00:11:08,502
"G" SHARP?

264
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:12,922
HAVE YOU BEEN STUDYING
THE REAL NAMES OF THE CHORDS?

265
00:11:14,174 --> 00:11:15,467
HAVE YOU?

266
00:11:16,635 --> 00:11:18,303
OH, MY GOD.

267
00:11:18,345 --> 00:11:20,597
WHAT? I-I DIDN'T
TOUCH A GUITAR!

268
00:11:20,639 --> 00:11:22,432
NO, BUT YOU'RE
QUESTIONING MY METHOD.

269
00:11:22,474 --> 00:11:24,476
NO. I'M NOT
QUESTIONING IT, PHOEBE.

270
00:11:24,518 --> 00:11:25,852
I'M SAYING
IT'S STUPID!

271
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:27,312
WHAT?

272
00:11:29,481 --> 00:11:30,773
THANK YOU.

273
00:11:31,983 --> 00:11:34,152
YOU KNOW, NONE OF
MY OTHER STUDENT

274
00:11:34,194 --> 00:11:36,446
THOUGHT I WAS STUPID!

275
00:11:37,489 --> 00:11:39,740
YOUR OTHER STUDENT
WAS YOU!

276
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:45,955
YEAH, WELL, YOU KNOW,
MAYBE YOU JUST NEED TO
TRY A LITTLE HARDER.

277
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:47,915
MAYBE I NEED TO TRY
A REAL TEACHER!

278
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:49,584
RIGHT HERE. HERE.
ANDY COOPER.

279
00:11:49,626 --> 00:11:51,002
HE TEACHES GUITAR.

280
00:11:51,044 --> 00:11:53,087
AND LOOK. OOH, THERE'S
A NICE PICTURE OF HIM

281
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:54,464
WITH A LITTLE KID, YEAH.

282
00:11:54,506 --> 00:11:56,424
AND THE KID'S GOT A GUITAR!

283
00:11:57,592 --> 00:11:59,135
FINE!

284
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:01,513
YOU GO LEARN FROM YOUR...
QUALIFIED INSTRUCTOR!

285
00:12:01,555 --> 00:12:03,014
BUT DON'T COME CRYING TO ME

286
00:12:03,056 --> 00:12:04,683
WHEN EVERYONE
IS SICK AND TIRED

287
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:07,060
OF HEARING YOU PLAY
"BAD, BAD, LEROY BROWN."

288
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:11,147
♪ BADDEST MAN
IN THE WHOLE DAMN TOWN... ♪

289
00:12:11,189 --> 00:12:13,483
OH, FINE. TAKE HIS SIDE!

290
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:22,200
Monica:
I can't wait to be with you.

291
00:12:22,242 --> 00:12:24,743
I'll sneak over
as soon as Ross picks up Ben.

292
00:12:24,785 --> 00:12:26,329
I'll just tell Rachel

293
00:12:26,371 --> 00:12:28,915
I'm going to be doing laundry
for a couple of hours.

294
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:31,710
Chandler:
Laundry? Huh.
Is that my new nickname?

295
00:12:34,713 --> 00:12:37,507
Monica:
You know what your nickname is,
Mr. Big...

296
00:12:37,549 --> 00:12:38,550
( shrieks )

297
00:12:48,101 --> 00:12:49,561
( phone ringing )

298
00:12:49,603 --> 00:12:50,978
HELLO.

299
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:53,772
JOEY, IT'S ROSS.
I NEED SOME HELP.

300
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:55,942
UH, CHANDLER'S NOT HERE.

301
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:57,694
WELL, YOU CAN HELP ME.

302
00:12:59,571 --> 00:13:00,821
OKAY.

303
00:13:00,863 --> 00:13:02,990
LISTEN, I'M IN
ELIZABETH'S BATHROOM...

304
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:05,493
NICE.

305
00:13:05,535 --> 00:13:07,995
NO, I GOT REALLY HOT
IN MY LEATHER PANTS

306
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:09,706
SO I TOOK THEM OFF

307
00:13:09,748 --> 00:13:12,667
BUT THEY MUST HAVE SHRUNK
FROM THE SWEAT OR SOMETHING

308
00:13:12,709 --> 00:13:16,170
OR MY LEGS EXPANDED
FROM THE HEAT.

309
00:13:16,212 --> 00:13:19,674
BUT I CAN'T GET THEM
BACK ON, JOEY.

310
00:13:19,716 --> 00:13:21,092
I CAN'T!

311
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:24,053
OH, THAT IS QUITE A SITUATION.

312
00:13:25,764 --> 00:13:28,683
UH, DO YOU SEE ANY,
LIKE, POWDER?

313
00:13:28,725 --> 00:13:30,644
POWDER, YEAH, YEAH.

314
00:13:30,685 --> 00:13:31,852
I HAVE POWDER.

315
00:13:31,894 --> 00:13:33,313
Good, good, okay.

316
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:34,564
SPRINKLE SOME
ON YOUR LEGS.

317
00:13:34,606 --> 00:13:36,107
IT WILL ABSORB SOME
OF THE MOISTURE

318
00:13:36,149 --> 00:13:37,734
AND THEN YOU CAN GET
YOUR PANTS ON.

319
00:13:37,776 --> 00:13:39,235
OKAY, HOLD ON.

320
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:05,178
THEY'RE NOT COMING ON, MAN.

321
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:08,348
UM, YOU SEE ANY... OH, VASELINE?

322
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:11,559
I... I SEE LOTION.

323
00:14:11,601 --> 00:14:12,727
I HAVE LOTION.

324
00:14:12,769 --> 00:14:14,061
WILL THAT WORK?

325
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:16,314
YEAH, SURE. THROW SOME
OF THAT ON THERE.

326
00:14:16,356 --> 00:14:17,607
Hold on.

327
00:14:31,705 --> 00:14:33,581
ROSS, YOU OKAY?

328
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:34,873
THEY'RE STILL...

329
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:37,168
THEY'RE STILL
NOT COMING ON, MAN.

330
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:40,755
AND THE LOTION AND THE POWDER
HAVE MADE A PASTE.

331
00:14:40,797 --> 00:14:42,256
REALLY?

332
00:14:42,298 --> 00:14:45,552
UH, WHAT COLOR IS IT?

333
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:49,305
WHAT DIFFERENCE
DOES THAT MAKE?

334
00:14:49,347 --> 00:14:51,057
WELL, IF THE PASTE
MATCHES THE PANTS

335
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:53,142
YOU CAN MAKE YOURSELF A PAIR
OF PASTE PANTS

336
00:14:53,184 --> 00:14:54,853
AND SHE WON'T KNOW
THE DIFFERENCE.

337
00:14:56,479 --> 00:14:58,272
JOEY, DO YOU
HAVE A MINUTE?

338
00:14:58,314 --> 00:14:59,816
DUDE, WHAT AM I...?

339
00:14:59,858 --> 00:15:01,526
RACHEL'S HERE.
SO GOOD LUCK, MAN.

340
00:15:01,568 --> 00:15:03,069
LET ME KNOW HOW
IT WORKS OUT.

341
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:07,073
OH, JOEY, I HAVE
SUCH A PROBLEM.

342
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:09,743
WELL, YOUR TIMING
COULDN'T BE BETTER.

343
00:15:09,784 --> 00:15:13,287
I AM PUTTING OUR FIRES
ALL OVER THE PLACE TODAY.

344
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:14,664
OKAY, OKAY, OKAY.

345
00:15:14,706 --> 00:15:17,958
JOEY, I HAVE GOT
TO TELL YOU SOMETHING.

346
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,293
WHAT? WHAT IS IT?
WHAT IS IT?

347
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:20,461
OH, MY GOD,
IT'S SO HUGE.

348
00:15:20,503 --> 00:15:22,004
BUT YOU JUST HAVE
TO PROMISE ME--

349
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:23,297
YOU CANNOT TELL ANYONE.

350
00:15:23,339 --> 00:15:24,965
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.
I DON'T WANT TO KNOW.

351
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:25,966
WHAT?

352
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:27,427
YES, YES, YES.

353
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:28,803
YOU DO WANT TO KNOW.
THIS IS UNBELIEVABLE.

354
00:15:28,845 --> 00:15:30,054
I DON'T CARE, RACHE.

355
00:15:30,096 --> 00:15:31,556
LOOK, I AM TIRED
OF BEING THE GUY

356
00:15:31,598 --> 00:15:34,100
WHO KNOWS ALL THE SECRETS
AND CAN'T TELL ANYONE.

357
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:35,810
YOU KNOW SECRETS?
WHAT ARE THEY?

358
00:15:35,852 --> 00:15:37,604
AND YOU'RE NOT SUPPOSED
TO BE GOSSIPING.

359
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,313
I KNOW, I JUST CAN'T
KEEP THIS ONE IN.

360
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:40,481
SO I PICK UP THE PHONE...

361
00:15:40,523 --> 00:15:42,483
( loud off-key singing )

362
00:15:44,694 --> 00:15:46,153
♪ LA-LA-LA-LA-LA! ♪

363
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:48,114
I'M NOT LISTENING
TO YOU.

364
00:15:48,155 --> 00:15:49,490
♪ AH-AH-AH-AH! ♪

365
00:15:49,532 --> 00:15:51,910
♪ AH! ♪

366
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:56,497
♪ AH... LA-LA-LA-LA! ♪

367
00:15:56,539 --> 00:15:57,624
( screams )

368
00:16:03,546 --> 00:16:08,342
ROSS, UM, YOU'VE BEEN IN THERE
FOR A LONG TIME.

369
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:11,262
I'M STARTING TO GET
KIND OF FREAKED OUT.

370
00:16:11,304 --> 00:16:13,848
ALL RIGHT,
I'M COMING OUT.

371
00:16:14,891 --> 00:16:17,059
HEY, CAN YOU TURN
THE LIGHTS OFF?

372
00:16:19,312 --> 00:16:20,605
NO.

373
00:16:20,647 --> 00:16:24,317
LET'S JUST LEAVE THE LIGHTS ON.

374
00:16:32,575 --> 00:16:34,911
OH, MY GOD.

375
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:37,997
I HAD A PROBLEM.

376
00:16:44,044 --> 00:16:45,379
HEY, PHEEBS.

377
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:47,381
OH, I CAN'T TALK TO YOU.

378
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:50,885
I DON'T HAVE A FANCY AD
IN THE YELLOW PAGES.

379
00:16:50,927 --> 00:16:54,430
LOOK, PHEEBS, I JUST...

380
00:16:54,472 --> 00:16:55,682
I WANT TO APOLOGIZE

381
00:16:55,723 --> 00:16:59,727
FOR SAYING YOUR
METHOD WAS STUPID

382
00:16:59,769 --> 00:17:01,980
AND MAYBE...

383
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:04,607
ASK YOU TO BE MY TEACHER AGAIN?

384
00:17:04,649 --> 00:17:06,943
AND-AND I PROMISE
I WON'T TOUCH A GUITAR

385
00:17:06,985 --> 00:17:08,486
UNTIL YOU SAY I'M READY.

386
00:17:17,662 --> 00:17:18,788
YOU REALLY THINK
I'M READY?

387
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:20,456
UH-HUH.

388
00:17:20,498 --> 00:17:22,792
WOW. COOL!

389
00:17:24,335 --> 00:17:25,628
OKAY.

390
00:17:28,422 --> 00:17:29,674
( dissonant clang )

391
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:45,105
WAS THE CHORD AT LEAST
RIGHT BEFORE...?

392
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:46,524
NO.

393
00:17:53,698 --> 00:17:56,868
OH, MY GOD!

394
00:17:56,910 --> 00:17:59,245
WE HEARD ABOUT YOUR PANTS.

395
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:00,580
I'M SO SORRY.

396
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:03,499
THIS YEAR WAS SUPPOSED
TO BE GREAT.

397
00:18:03,541 --> 00:18:05,125
WELL, IT'S ONLY
THE SECOND DAY

398
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:09,129
AND I'M A LOSER
WITH STUPID LEATHER PANTS

399
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:11,131
THAT DON'T EVEN FIT!

400
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:13,009
NO, YOU'RE
NOT A LOSER.

401
00:18:13,051 --> 00:18:14,343
( all murmur agreement )

402
00:18:14,385 --> 00:18:16,721
LOOK AT ME!

403
00:18:16,763 --> 00:18:18,389
( squeaks )

404
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:25,396
HEY, HEY, LOOK.
LOOK, ROSS.

405
00:18:25,438 --> 00:18:27,690
BEN DREW A PICTURE OF YOU.

406
00:18:27,732 --> 00:18:29,609
HUH? YOU'RE A COWBOY.

407
00:18:32,403 --> 00:18:34,030
OH.

408
00:18:34,072 --> 00:18:36,699
BE-BECAUSE OF
THE LEATHER PANTS?

409
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:40,078
SEE? BEN DOESN'T THINK
YOU'RE A LOSER.

410
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:41,412
HE THINKS YOU'RE A COWBOY.

411
00:18:41,454 --> 00:18:42,747
I MEAN, THAT'S SOMETHING.

412
00:18:42,789 --> 00:18:44,206
( all murmur agreement )

413
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:46,960
HOWDY, PARTNER.
HEY-HEY.

414
00:18:47,001 --> 00:18:49,169
MAYBE I SHOULD GET
ANOTHER PAIR.

415
00:18:49,211 --> 00:18:52,924
OOH! YOU KNOW, THEY
HAD SOME WITH, UH...

416
00:18:52,966 --> 00:18:56,302
WITH FRINGE
ALL DOWN THE SIDES.

417
00:18:58,429 --> 00:19:00,014
I'M GOING TO GO
KISS BEN GOOD NIGHT.

418
00:19:03,935 --> 00:19:08,106
I CAN'T BELIEVE
HE THINKS I'M A COWBOY.

419
00:19:08,188 --> 00:19:10,900
I WOULD MAKE A GOOD COWBOY.

420
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:17,031
OKAY, NOW THAT
EVERYTHING'S
WRAPPED UP HERE

421
00:19:17,073 --> 00:19:19,742
I THINK I'M GOING
TO GO DO MY LAUNDRY.

422
00:19:19,784 --> 00:19:21,577
ME, TOO, YOU KNOW, IF
THIS SHIRT IS DIRTY.

423
00:19:21,619 --> 00:19:22,870
YEP.

424
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:31,295
HEY, I'M GOING
TO GO, TOO.

425
00:19:31,337 --> 00:19:32,964
I'M GOING TO GO TO THE AIRPORT.

426
00:19:33,006 --> 00:19:35,215
I FIGURE IF I HANG ROUND THERE
LONG ENOUGH

427
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:38,260
SOMEONE'S BOUND TO LEAVE
ONE OF THOSE PLANES UNATTENDED.

428
00:19:38,302 --> 00:19:40,220
GOOD LUCK, HONEY.
BYE.

429
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:42,348
( door closes )

430
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:44,767
WOW.

431
00:19:44,809 --> 00:19:46,560
HEY, UH, JOEY,
REMEMBER THAT BIG THING

432
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:47,979
I WAS GOING TO TELL YOU ABOUT?

433
00:19:48,021 --> 00:19:49,105
OH, NO.

434
00:19:49,147 --> 00:19:50,898
( singing loud gibberish )

435
00:19:51,899 --> 00:19:53,109
I'M NOT GOING
TO TELL YOU

436
00:19:53,151 --> 00:19:54,819
BUT IF YOU FOUND OUT ON YOUR OWN

437
00:19:54,861 --> 00:19:57,196
THAT WOULD BE OKAY, AND THEN
WE COULD TALK ABOUT IT, RIGHT?

438
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:59,281
WELL,
THEN IT WOULDN'T BE A SECRET

439
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:01,117
SO, YEAH, THAT WOULD BE OKAY.

440
00:20:01,159 --> 00:20:02,326
YEAH, YEAH.

441
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:04,871
YEAH.

442
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:07,123
HEY, UH, JOE, WOULD
YOU MIND GOING OVER

443
00:20:07,165 --> 00:20:10,084
INTO CHANDLER'S BEDROOM
AND GETTING THAT BOOK BACK

444
00:20:10,126 --> 00:20:12,294
THAT HE BORROWED
FROM ME?

445
00:20:15,173 --> 00:20:17,884
NOW? YOU WANT ME
TO GO OVER THERE NOW?

446
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:19,468
HMM.

447
00:20:19,510 --> 00:20:21,179
DO YOU KNOW SOMETHING?

448
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:23,181
DO YOU KNOW SOMETHING?

449
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:24,849
I MIGHT KNOW SOMETHING.

450
00:20:24,891 --> 00:20:26,517
I MIGHT KNOW SOMETHING, TOO.

451
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:28,019
WHAT'S THE THING YOU KNOW?

452
00:20:28,061 --> 00:20:29,645
I CAN'T TELL YOU
TILL YOU TELL ME.

453
00:20:29,687 --> 00:20:30,563
I CAN'T TELL YOU.

454
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:31,313
I CAN'T TELL YOU.

455
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,606
OKAY, FINE.

456
00:20:40,823 --> 00:20:43,617
YOU DON'T KNOW.

457
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:45,912
HOW ABOUT I GO OVER AND
WALK INTO CHANDLER'S BEDROOM

458
00:20:45,953 --> 00:20:47,538
AND SEE THE THING
I THINK THAT I KNOW

459
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,456
IS ACTUALLY THE THING
I THINK THAT I KNOW.

460
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:50,624
( gasps )

461
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:52,001
YOU KNOW!

462
00:20:52,043 --> 00:20:52,919
AND YOU KNOW!

463
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,170
YEAH, I KNOW!

464
00:20:54,212 --> 00:20:55,671
CHANDLER AND MONICA?!

465
00:20:55,713 --> 00:20:57,297
OH, THIS IS UNBELIEVABLE!

466
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:58,674
HOW LONG HAVE YOU KNOWN?!

467
00:20:58,716 --> 00:21:00,051
TOO LONG! OH,
MY GOD, RACHE!

468
00:21:00,093 --> 00:21:02,011
I'VE BEEN DYING TO TALK
TO SOMEONE ABOUT THIS

469
00:21:02,053 --> 00:21:03,137
FOR SO LONG!

470
00:21:03,179 --> 00:21:04,263
BUT LISTEN, LISTEN.

471
00:21:04,304 --> 00:21:05,848
YOU CAN'T SAY
ANYTHING TO ANYBODY.

472
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:07,307
THEY'RE SO WEIRD ABOUT THAT.

473
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:08,559
LISTEN...

474
00:21:08,601 --> 00:21:09,518
( yelling )
( yelling )

475
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:11,020
HEY, PHOEBE!

476
00:21:11,062 --> 00:21:12,396
HEY. IT'S RAINING.

477
00:21:12,438 --> 00:21:14,982
I DON'T LIKE TO FLY
IN THE RAIN, SO...

478
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:18,236
OH!

479
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:20,863
I AM GOING TO GO FOR
A WALK IN THE RAIN.

480
00:21:20,905 --> 00:21:22,281
OH, YEAH, ME, TOO.

481
00:21:26,368 --> 00:21:28,204
THAT'S WEIRD.

482
00:21:28,246 --> 00:21:30,957
I BET THEY'RE DOING IT.

483
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:38,756
OH, GOOD. OKAY, LOOK,
I CAN'T TAKE IT ANYMORE.

484
00:21:38,798 --> 00:21:43,052
I CAN'T TAKE IT ANYMORE,
SO YOU WIN, OKAY? HERE.

485
00:21:43,094 --> 00:21:44,220
PHEEBS, FLYING A JET?

486
00:21:44,262 --> 00:21:45,972
BETTER MAKE IT A SPACESHIP

487
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:48,682
SO YOU CAN GET BACK
TO YOUR HOME PLANET.

488
00:21:50,268 --> 00:21:52,019
AND ROSS,
PHONE CALL FOR YOU TODAY.

489
